{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CjEfVZmUrSSd4WKA8e7Rdr","type":"tool_result","content":"- [ ] **11 Reserve.** The best remaining gap from items 01–10, one session,\n  chosen in this order of value and stated in PROGRESS.md with the reason:\n  (1) a Lean gap left by 06–09 (R3–R4, the regular case of S1, C2); (2)\n  Fomin–Høie's Lemma 4 in Lean for maximum degree 3 — the statement with\n  `X` as the end bag, `tree_pathwidth_le_log` as its tree case, the three\n  cases of its proof — which with C1 and a stated Monien–Preis bisection\n  would make the base case itself conditional only on the bisection\n  theorem; (3) the per-step `pw(H) ≤ pw(H') + 1` for one series-parallel\n  operation (unconditional, cheap, and *not* the reduction lemma — say so),\n  with the measured `pw(H) − pw(r(H))` of item 02 extended to 10 vertices;\n  (4) Theorem 5.3's averaging lemma fetched from Edwards & Farr 2012 (EJC,\n  open) and checked on the record. Compute at most 1 core-hour; nothing\n  proved is re-solved.\n====\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Regression gate for loop0012 (the Edwards–McDermid degree-sequence bound).\n\nPasses only if all five hold:\n1. `lake build` in lean/ succeeds;\n2. every `.lean` file under lean/MOSPFormalization/ (top level, Complex/ and\n   Search/) is imported by lean/MOSPFormalization.lean, so the build really\n   checks it;\n3. the number of `sorry` in Lean *code* (comments and docstrings stripped) is\n   at most the baseline (0: the development has none since Appendix E) plus\n   the entries in allowed_sorries.txt, and no `axiom` declaration exists;\n4. `python -m pytest tests/ -q -x` passes, and so does `pytest` in\n   pathwidth_solver/;\n5. the paper builds with no undefined references (`make -C paper1/latex check`).\n\n    python3 Ralph_Loops/loop0012/gate.py\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport re\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nHERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nREPO = HERE.parents[1]\nLEAN = REPO / \"lean\"\nBASELINE_SORRIES = 0\nALLOWED = HERE / \"allowed_sorries.txt\"\nPAPER = REPO / \"paper1\" / \"latex\"\n\n\ndef strip_comments(src: str) -> str:\n    out, i, depth = [], 0, 0\n    while i < len(src):\n        if src.startswith(\"/-\", i):\n            depth += 1; i += 2; continue\n        if depth and src.startswith(\"-/\", i):\n            depth -= 1; i += 2; continue\n        if depth:\n            i += 1; continue\n        if src.startswith(\"--\", i):\n            j = src.find(\"\\n\", i); i = len(src) if j < 0 else j; continue\n        if src[i] == '\"':\n            j = i + 1\n            while j < len(src) and src[j] != '\"':\n                j += 2 if src[j] == \"\\\\\" else 1\n            i = j + 1; continue\n        out.append(src[i]); i += 1\n    return \"\".join(out)\n\n\ndef main() -> int:\n    ok = True\n    b = subprocess.run([\"lake\", \"build\"], cwd=LEAN, capture_output=True, text=True, errors=\"replace\")\n    tail = \"\\n\".join((b.stdout + b.stderr).splitlines()[-25:])\n    if b.returncode != 0:\n        print(\"GATE FAIL: lake build\\n\" + tail); return 1\n    print(\"lake build: ok\")\n\nPages:           74\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 al al 878342 Nov  2 00:46 paper1/latex/main.pdf\nMon Nov 2 06:15:59 2026 +0000","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"97b23e8b-c280-4820-b777-f4948c9a83ab","uuid":"076b644b-687d-4ea1-84c4-2175c8aba514","timestamp":"2026-11-02T06:16:36.511Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"- [ ] **11 Reserve.** The best remaining gap from items 01–10, one session,\n  chosen in this order of value and stated in PROGRESS.md with the reason:\n  (1) a Lean gap left by 06–09 (R3–R4, the regular case of S1, C2); (2)\n  Fomin–Høie's Lemma 4 in Lean for maximum degree 3 — the statement with\n  `X` as the end bag, `tree_pathwidth_le_log` as its tree case, the three\n  cases of its proof — which with C1 and a stated Monien–Preis bisection\n  would make the base case itself conditional 